# The storeclass lint: its analyzer, baseline, ceiling, allowlist, sealed
# lists and generator. Raising raw-store debt, or weakening what the lint
# sees, is a coordinator decision (tools/nogo/analyzers/storeclass).
/tools/nogo/analyzers/storeclass/ @gastownhall/gascity-admin
# What makes nogo run it: the analyzer set, the nogo target, and the rules_go
# patches that make nolint unable to suppress storeclass and feed it the
# baseline. MODULE.bazel's rules_go override and go_sdk.nogo registration, and
# config.json's _base and storeclass scopes, are guarded by the storeclass
# growth gate instead (cmd/storeclass-baseline wirings): owning those files
# whole would put every dependency bump and every other analyzer's settings
# behind an admin review.
/tools/nogo/analyzers.bzl @gastownhall/gascity-admin
/tools/nogo/BUILD.bazel @gastownhall/gascity-admin
/third_party/patches/rules_go_nogo_golangci_nolint.patch @gastownhall/gascity-admin
/third_party/patches/rules_go_nogo_main_repo_data.patch @gastownhall/gascity-admin
/contrib/k8s/ @gastownhall/gascity-admin
